                <pb facs="0742" n="606" sameAs="frus:frus1929v01/pg606"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">810.79611 Pan American Airways, Inc./719:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Guatemala</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Hawks</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-11-18T15:00:00-05:00">November 18, 1929—3
                        p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>71. Your 148, November 14, 3 p.m. Provided that it will not conflict with any
                    existing contracts or pending application of other American countries [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">companies?</hi>] you are authorized to do as requested
                    on behalf of the Pan American Airways, Incorporated, but not of its non-American
                    subsidiary.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
